---
title: Operations on quantities
summary: The operation crates. skoro-linalg (matmul, transpose, norms, cross products, Tril, fixed and sparse linear maps), skoro-pointwise, skoro-so3 and skoro-se3.
order: 8
---

Each crate on this page adds `DiffOperation`s and exposes them on typed handles through `*Ops`
extension traits (and operator overloads where natural).

## `skoro-linalg`

- `Matmul`, `Transpose`, `CrossProduct`, vector norms.
- `Tril`, the manifold of lower-triangular matrices, used for covariance factors.
- `FixedLinearMap` / `linear_map` applies a host-supplied matrix as a differentiable operation. This
  is how a builder without access to constants (a distribution) puts a known matrix into the graph.
- `SparseLinearMap` / `sparse_linear_map` does the same for a large sparse matrix, storing only its
  nonzeros. The Gaussian Fisher root is built this way.

These are *differentiable graph operations*. The dense factorizations an estimator needs are a
separate concern ([Host linear algebra](../host-linear-algebra/)).

## `skoro-pointwise`

Elementwise `log` and `abs` on `Real` and Euclidean quantities.

## `skoro-so3`

The rotation group, stored as a flattened $3\times3$ matrix: `exp` (Rodrigues' formula), `log`,
retraction and inverse retraction, compose, rotate/unrotate, and invert.

## `skoro-se3`

Rigid-body transforms (rotation plus translation), built by composing the SO(3) operations with
translation.

